WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.080
- I should probably not tell this story,

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.739
but this is who I am.

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:06.322
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.920
I'm looking forward to actually having

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.070
more guests back, like in person.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.210
I feel like I got to talk

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.070
to a lot of people in second season

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.880
that maybe wouldn't have
been able to come to the show

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.180
or don't really travel,

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.900
but like, I got to talk to Michael Douglas

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.190
and Catherine Zeta-Jones in Spain.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.610
I got to talk to Julie Andrews.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.730
I got to talk to all
these people that I love

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.020
that maybe wouldn't have come on the show,

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.380
maybe in second season,
because of whatever reason,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.370
and because of how we were remote,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.100
I got to really connect
with a lot of people

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.540
that maybe wouldn't have
come on the show before.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.510
So it was really cool to
kinda meet those people

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.240
and establish those relationships,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.490
and now maybe get to have them in person,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.870
because like, do I wanna hug Julie Andrews

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:53.290
like an awkward amount of time?

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.220
Yes, I do.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.620
I think I'm excited to have
people that I had over like,

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.720
whatever on the screen.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.260
I'm excited to have them
back here in person.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.920
That's kind of what
I'm super stoked about,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.500
and I'm excited about Kellyokes
again, I like doing them.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.757
And by the end of last season I was like,

00:01:07.757 --> 00:01:09.540
"Oh my God," my brain was exploding,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.373
'cause we've done so many,

00:01:10.373 --> 00:01:12.150
there's a hundred and
eighty every season y'all,

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.340
it's a lot of songs.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.010
But I think I've had enough of a break

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.174
to where I'm like stoked again, so...

00:01:18.174 --> 00:01:20.757
(upbeat music)

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.020
So I think this season we
already have a ton picked

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.020
for next season,

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.650
but we had a lot of requests

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:33.050
for people to actually
have me sing my songs,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:36.680
and I think that's
weird, because it's vain.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.110
And like I'm gonna open
the show with my song,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.760
and like if it's not
a new song coming out.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.920
But I listened,

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.830
so my musical director,
Jason, and I were talking

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.450
and we might do...

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.020
We're gonna sprinkle in
some of my like songs

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.340
that people maybe wanna hear
that haven't heard in a while

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.450
because I haven't been doing shows.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.630
We're gonna sprinkle it in and do...

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.070
How they win me over is
we're gonna twist it up.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.830
We're gonna do them a little differently,

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.090
than maybe you've heard them before.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.880
So that will be exciting
and kinda cool to do.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.050
And we already have a
huge list of Kellyokes

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.590
that we've picked several that
we're gonna kinda change up.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:11.940
I like doing that, we can't do it

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.930
for all hundred and eighty
'cause there's not enough time,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.290
but I like when we have the
time to really take a song

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.930
and like flip it a little bit.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.718
But yeah, I'm excited about Kellyokes.

00:02:19.718 --> 00:02:22.301
(upbeat music)

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.060
I should probably not tell this story,

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.510
but this is who I am.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.350
One of the funniest things that's happened

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.500
on this show this far, in any season,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.500
was I was doing a juice
cleanse and... (laughs)

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.950
And, I think it was Whitney
Cummings who was there.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:43.200
And I think it was Whitney
Cummings' worst time.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.957
And I literally looked at her and I go,

00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:46.710
"Yeah," I was like, "I
just, I'll be right back."

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.877
And then I like ran to the bathroom,

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.680
and then I came back and I
just broke it down for Whitney.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.987
I felt like we could be
those girls, and I was like,

00:02:54.987 --> 00:02:59.170
"Whoa! I had to go because
I'm choosing work time

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.830
to do a juice cleanse apparently,

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.510
and it caught up with me.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.572
And so, (bleeping) happens."

00:03:05.572 --> 00:03:08.052
(laughs)
(crowd laughs)

00:03:08.052 --> 00:03:10.583
And that was pretty much
the most memorable...

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.420
Other than that, there
was one time we learned...

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.900
This is also one I shouldn't probably say.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.800
Sometimes we have to do the Kellyokes last

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.130
because of whatever timing
or a guest needs to go,

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.380
something happens, so
we have to do it last.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.840
Well, everyone sells an alcohol, right,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.270
like everyone that comes on here,

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.930
and I don't wanna lie so like, I try it,

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.770
so I'm like, and it's
usually a little bit,

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.510
so it's like fine.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.210
This particular day I did not remember

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.200
that I had not had dinner the night before

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.440
because of kid stuff,
whatever, running around.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.800
And I had not had breakfast,
and obviously not lunch,

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:45.960
'cause it was kind of lunchtime,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.430
we were wrapping up the show,

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.330
I was about to have lunch.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.610
So I didn't have food, and I was trying...

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:54.990
I can't even remember
whose alcohol it was,

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.130
but I'll tell you what (laughs)

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.380
I know it was a Toni Braxton song,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.010
and it was "You mean
the world to me" maybe,

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.510
I don't know which one it was.

00:04:05.727 --> 00:04:09.310
It was like climbing Mount
Everest to get that song.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.297
It had affected me till I was like,

00:04:11.297 --> 00:04:12.980
"Oh my God, I can't."

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.420
I felt like I was at a karaoke bar,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.870
and I'd had a couple.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.950
And I, which is not great.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.600
And it took me a minute
to get that Kellyoke done,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.910
and I think we've realized, one,

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.050
try and get Kellyokes done
at the very beginning.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:30.060
And then two, maybe just take a tiny sip,

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.360
to be honest and say,

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.113
you either liked or disliked
their alcohol flavor, or,

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.280
eat beforehand.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.520
So that was fun too, but "You
mean the world", it was...

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.110
I was sweating. It was sad. (laughs)

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:47.040
It was sad. But we got it done.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.910
I think it was Dwayne Johnson's tequila,

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.773
which I'm gonna be honest
with you, is so good.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:56.990
To Dwayne Johnson
everybody! (crowd cheers)

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.840
It was a really big
shock, and then it's like,

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.480
I'm on camera, I'm like,
we'll I don't wanna look weak.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.545
So I'm like, "I can do this,"
and then I was like "Whoa."

00:05:06.545 --> 00:05:09.680
(upbeat music)

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.340
I mean, I think everyone knows
the answer to this question,

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.550
but I'm kind of half and half,

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.540
because I'm nervous about it.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.510
But I think a dream surprise for me,

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.320
I know they surprised me
last year with Patty Griffin,

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.640
which I was floored, I
was like, there's a...

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.220
She has a doppelganger.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.070
The amount of time it
took me to figure out

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.060
it was actually Patty Griffin.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.140
I was like, "What?"

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.310
First of all, holy (bleep)! Holy (bleep)!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.986
I was like, she looks
exactly like Patty Griffin!

00:05:38.986 --> 00:05:40.673
(screams)

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.423
Like I was freaking out.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:45.890
I think that, yeah,

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.500
the person who would probably
freak me out the most

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.680
would probably be Meryl Streep,

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.423
but here's the thing,

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.520
I'm on the fence over that really,

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.290
'cause like you know when
you love someone so much

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.610
and you're just so,

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.010
you adore them so much that you're like,

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:59.900
maybe we shouldn't ever really...

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.580
We met, like quickly on a red carpet,

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.640
but I just mean like,

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.330
like sit and chat, I don't know,

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.530
I think I might be nervous.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.100
Or Julie Andrews in person, what!

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.510
I would be really happy about that.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.890
There's a lot of people honestly
I'd be very excited about,

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.110
I like a lot of people.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.730
But I think that like ultimate for me,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:19.730
just because how much I
watch her films and love her,

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:20.783
also it's 'cause,

00:06:20.783 --> 00:06:22.310
you know what, y'all,
she's not just a singer,

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.660
she's like a dancer, she's
an actor, a singer, a dancer.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:27.950
Meryl is everything.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.700
Like, not many people are everything.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.781
That's a lot of talent in
one human, just saying.

00:06:33.781 --> 00:06:36.364
(upbeat music)

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.640
(signal beeps)
(indistinct chatter)

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.270
I'm sorry.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.299
It's this one? It's...

00:06:45.299 --> 00:06:47.021
You know what is funny?
It's probably not even mine.

00:06:47.021 --> 00:06:48.050
(crowd laughs)
I mean it's mine,

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.883
I bought it.
(signal beeps)

